  "report_period": "Week 46 (12th Nov to 19th Nov 2021)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Panamax \"Yutai Ambitions\" 77/2008 Oshima, Japan (SS/DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) was committed to Greek buyers for USD 18,7 mill. For reference, the \"Okeanos Bliss\" 76/2008 Imabari, Japan (SS 11/2023, DD 10/2021) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 18,75 mill basis delivery October-November 2021 with DD passed & BWTS fitted. Moreover, the vintage \"Braveheart\" 74/2001 Imabari, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 05/2024, BWTS fitted) from AM Nomikos was committed for USD 13 mill. For comparison, the \"Banasol\" 72/2001 Oshima, Japan (SS 01/2026, DD 01/2024, BWTS fitted) was sold a month ago at USD 14 mill. Grieg Star AS sold to Greek buyers their Ultramax sister vessels \"Star Crios\" 63/2012 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 06/2022) for USD 21,5 mill basis prompt delivery Far East & the \"Star Damon\" 63/2012 Yangzhou, China (SS/DD 10/2022, BWTS fitted) for USD 22,5 mill with T/C attached until March-May 2022 at 36.000 usd/pd. Japanese owners sold their OHBS Handysize \"Royal Justice\" 37/2012 Saiki, Japan (SS/DD 12/2022, BWTS fitted) to undisclosed buyers for region USD 19,5 mill. Note that the \"Crest Navigator\" 36/2012 Shikoku, Japan (SS 10/2025, DD 11/2023, BWTS fitted) was sold three weeks ago at USD 21,5 mill.",
    "tankers": "Maran Tankers have sold their VLCC \"Maran Corona\" 306/2003 Daewoo, Korea (SS 07/2023, DD 12/2021) for USD 28,5 mill. Latest similar sale was the one-year-younger \"Gilos\" 319/2004 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS 10/2024, DD 08/2022), which was sold a month ago at USD 29 mill. The Suezmax \"Densa Whale\" 158/2012 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 03/2022, BWTS fitted) from Marinsa Denizcilik was sold to Greek buyers Thenamaris for region USD 32 mill. Hyundai Glovis committed their two MR2 sister vessels \"PTI Rhine\" & \"PTI Amazon\" 51/2007 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 02/2022 & SS/DD 03/2022 respectively) to undisclosed buyers for USD 9,9 mill each. Note that a couple of weeks ago, the sister vessel \"Star Eagle\" 51/2007 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 10/2022) was sold at USD 11,75 mill. Furthermore, the MR1 \"Seaways Bodie\" 37/2006 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 01/2022) was committed for USD 7,6 mill, while the \"Aiolos\" 37/2007 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 03/2022) was sold three weeks ago at USD 8 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of mid/high usd 10,00's fio range. A number of round trips on the same route were reported around usd 23,000/24,000 pd levels. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 19,000/21,000 pd. CIS Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 16,000/18,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed around usd 14,000/15,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were fixed around usd 20,000/23,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips via Black Sea into China were fixed around usd 21,000 pd. West African trips via East Coast South America into Continent were reported at the level of usd 20,000/21,500 pd. Inter-Continental trips via Murmansk were fixed around usd 29,000/30,000 pd. Continental trips via US Gulf into China were reported at the level of usd 30,000/32,000 pd. Mediterranean trips via Black Sea into Continent were fixed around usd 29,000/31,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 30,000/32,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 17,000/20,000 pd range. West Coast Indian trips into South East Asia were reported at the level of usd 29,000/31,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into China with steel billets were fixed around usd 30,000 pd. Persian Gulf trips into East Coast India were reported at the level of usd 27,000/28,000 pd. South African trips into China with manganese ore were fixed around usd 24,500 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 1.45M. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "South East Asian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 24,000 pd. West African trips via Continent into Caribbean were fixed around usd 30,000/32,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Caribbean with aggregates were reported at the level of usd 30,000/32,000 pd. A number of trips from US East Coast into Continent with woodpellets were fixed around usd 27,000/29,000 pd. North Coast South American trips into US East Coast were reported at the level of usd 26,000/28,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
